# open62541-qnx change: tcp-accept-aborted
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
#
# title: Keep the listen socket when accept() finds an aborted connection
# file: open62541.c
# upstream: arch/eventloop_posix_tcp.c
# test: robust.aborted_connect
#
# When accept() fails with anything but EINTR, the listen socket is closed
# and the server accepts no connection any more until it is restarted.
#
# A connection that the peer resets while it waits in the listen queue is such
# a failure on a BSD network stack: accept() returns ECONNABORTED, or the
# stack has already removed the connection and the non-blocking accept()
# returns EWOULDBLOCK. Linux hands out the dead connection instead, so the
# problem does not show there. One TCP handshake followed by a reset is all
# that a peer needs to send.
#
@@ hunk
